{title: I Am Joseph}
{subtitle: Genesis 45:1–8; 50:20}
{key: D}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [D] | [D] | [D] |
| [D] | [D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Make everyone go out from me
And no one stayed with him
He wept so loudly that Egypt heard
I am Joseph, is my father still alive
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
His brothers could not answer him
They were dismayed at his presence
Come near to me, please, he said
I am your brother whom you sold into Egypt
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Do [G]not be distressed or [A]angry with yourselves
[Bm7]God sent me before you to [D]preserve life
You [G]meant evil against me
But [A]God meant it for [D]good
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
So it was not you who sent me here, but God
He has made me a father to Pharaoh
Hurry and go up to my father
And tell him, come down to me, do not tarry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Do [G]not be distressed or [A]angry with yourselves
God [Bm7]sent me before you to pre[D]serve life
You [G]meant evil against me
But [A]God meant it for [D]good
{end_of_chorus}
